.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-server-rdns-list - List reverse DNS entries


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server rdns list  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List reverse DNS entries

.PP
\fBtr-ist-1 (Gyro Bulut İstanbul):\fP every address (primary and additional IPv4) gets an automatic PTR \fB<a-b-c-d>.ip.gyrohosting.com\fR with a matching A record. Set \fBhostname\fR to your own FQDN to replace it (published within seconds); an empty value restores the default. Names under Gyro domains and protected brand names are refused (HTTP 422 with an explanatory message); at most 30 changes per server per hour. The A record of your name should point to the address (forward-confirmed reverse DNS) for e-mail delivery; it is not enforced. When the server is deleted or an additional IP is released, its PTR is removed.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/servers/{id}/rdns (operationId listRdns, scope cloud_read)


